# enrichment's lead routes (core/modules/enrichment/README.md "The lead page"): a member's session,
# enrichment.read for the GET and enrichment.run for the POST. The GET answers the person's
# company facts and country, each with its source class and when, an empty one null, and the
# person's last run; never a provider's name. The POST asks for a run now, free: 202 with the run
# and its status, queued; the worker runs it and the GET then answers it done with the fields it
# filled. The Idempotency-Key is an example UUID and the run's request key too: the same one
# answers the same run. A write sends the cookie, so it sends Origin: {{appOrigin}} too. Put in
# http-client.private.env.json, with your workspaceId: `personId`, a lead of yours. Refusals: 404
# enrichment_person_not_found (another workspace's person, an unknown one), 400
# idempotency_key_required.

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/enrichment/leads/{personId}: the company's facts, the lead's country and the last run
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/enrichment/leads/{{personId}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/enrichment/leads/{personId}: asks for a run now; 202, queued
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/enrichment/leads/{{personId}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
Idempotency-Key: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000550
